 "notes": "Stretch 3. p.121 starts at the row below the long rule (y~890) '1. Re en erṭāt ...'; rows above not read. p.122 read to the last row ending 'χāāu - f' (English 'his ..........'); nothing printed below it. Line numerals: CXXXII — '1.' at the left margin before Re (p.121 row 1); '2.' before per (p.121 row 2, after the Lion-god group); '3.' at the start of p.122 row 1 before maat. Chapter X — '1.' before ki (p.122 title row); '2.' printed inside ba - nà between the jabiru and the vulture (word keeps line 1; χut is line 2); '3.' before às (p.122 row 5, after nuk); '4.' before às (p.122 row 6, after nuk). Overlines: the title rows of both chapters have no overline other than the long chapter rule directly above them; short overlines start the following rows over 't'eṭ àn' (p.121 row 2, ends before Àusàr) and over 'neter - χert' (p.122 row 4), so I treated the long rule as the title overline and marked the titles rubric (flagged in 'unsure' on the first title word). Dots: p.121 row 2 Budge prints '....' as transliteration for the lion + seated figure group ('the Lion-god'); p.122 last row English 'his ..........' (translation left blank for χāāu - f). (sic): p.122 row 5, above the viper I9 of re - f. Brackets in the sign line: p.122 row 1 [D21] er; p.122 row 6 erṭā - n[A1]; p.122 row 7 Ani [A1]. No footnotes in this stretch. Budge's p.122 row 2 'ḥetep' is broken in print ('ḥet:p')."
